{"benchmark": "ifeval", "task_id": "1001", "sample_idx": 4, "model_name": "mistralai/ministral-14b-instruct-2512", "content": "Hark ye traveler bold who dost set sail for Japan’s fair shores\nLet this itinerary be thy guide through lands of grace and lore\n\n**Upon thy first morn in Tokyo’s bustling embrace**\nAwake where cherry blossoms kiss the sun’s bright face\nDo walk through Ueno’s park where temples old do stand\nBehold the shrine of Asakusa where lanterns softly planned\n\n**In midday’s glow proceed to Asakusa’s heart**\nWhere Sensoji’s gate doth guard with golden hues so art\nPartake of tempura’s delight or ramen’s warm embrace\nLet merchants’ cries fill thy ears in this mercantile place\n\n**When evening’s shroud doth fall upon the city’s spire**\nTo Shinjuku’s lights thou must repair\nOdaiba’s bay shall greet thee with wonders grand and wide\nAkihabara’s glow doth call with neon bright by night\n\n**On morn of the second day be swift and true**\nTo Harajuku’s streets where fashion’s wild wind blows anew\nTake heed of Takeshita’s Street where quirks in colors play\nThen cross the river to Meiji’s shrine where gods hold sway\n\n**When Shibuya’s scramble cross thou dost behold**\nA dance of souls in streets both wide and bold\nClimb to Yoyogi’s hills for rest beneath the breeze\nThen dine where izakayas hum with tales of old Japan’s ease\n\n**Awake anew and board the train swift and keen**\nTo Nikko’s forests where temples echo through the green\nKegon Falls do whisper secrets to the ancient stone\nToshogu’s shrine shall leave thy heart both full and grown\n\n**Return to Tokyo’s heart where one more night thou’ll spend**\nIn Ginza’s glow where lanterns dance and jewels shall bend\nThen rest thy head for morn’s next call to Kyoto’s embrace\n\n**Upon the third dawn let Kyoto’s grace be thy delight**\nFushimi’s shrine where bells in morning’s hush take flight\nGion’s streets where geisha glide with steps both soft and light\nKinkaku-ji’s gold shall dazzle day or night\n\n**Do walk where Arashiyama’s bamboo sways in prayer**\nAnd cross the bridge of t’angel’s breath where time doth slow to snare\nVisit Kiyomizu’s stage where monks once chanted lore\nThen sample matcha’s green in tea houses evermore\n\n**When twilight paints the sky in hues of purple hue**\nTo Pontocho’s alley where lanterns dangle anew\nBehold the moon above Nijo’s castle’s grand display\nThen lose thyself in Kyoto’s charm night’s dark ballet\n\n**On morn of the fourth let Kyoto’s wonders take their leave**\nTo Nara’s dawn where deer in sacred grounds do rove\nTodai-ji’s Buddha smiles with wisdom old and true\nThen ride the train once more to Osaka’s lively hue\n\n**In Osaka’s heart let feasts of joy thy soul fulfill**\nBehold the castle where heroes’ deeds in legends twirl\nDotonbori’s lights shall make thy taste buds yearn for more\nTry takoyaki’s bite or okonomiyaki’s lore\n\n**When thy belly’s full and laughter fills the air**\nTo Universal’s realm of fantasy repair\nThen stroll through Osaka’s lanes where history doth hum\nBefore thy final night in Osaka’s brightest gleam\n\n**Awake one last morn and take the train once more**\nTo Hiroshima’s shores where peace doth stand forevermore\nMiyajima’s torii in the bay shall rise from sea’s embrace\nThen touch the park where silence speaks of souls at peace\n\n**Return to Tokyo’s arms where thy grand voyage must end**\nAt Narita’s gate bid farewell to lands without end\nWith memories of temples shrines and feasts both bold and sweet\nGo forth with heart both full and soul in Japan’s enchantment complete.", "logprobs": [{"token": "H", "logprob": -0.16147485375404358}, {"token": "ark", "logprob": -0.004245435819029808}, {"token": " ye", "logprob": -3.3954992294311523}, {"token": " travel", "logprob": -0.4291493594646454}, {"token": "er", "logprob": -0.00038115866482257843}, {"token": " bold", "logprob": -0.46826794743537903}, {"token": " who", "logprob": -0.9528059363365173}, {"token": " dost", "logprob": -0.2